#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:331
msgid "Search persons"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:332
msgid "Searches Orbis persons and returns their contact details, organization, gender and birth date. Without a search term all persons are returned, ordered by name. Upcoming birthdays are persons ordered by \"birthday\": the person whose birthday is next comes first. The output contains the current date of the site. Use orbis-persons/get for the full description of a person and orbis/search-comments for the comments of a person."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:340
msgid "Search term, matched against the display name, the first names, the last names, the email addresses, the organization and the phone numbers."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:344
msgid "Limit the results to persons with this gender: the ID, slug or name of a term of the gender taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:348
msgid "Sort the persons by name, creation date, modification date or upcoming birthday. Persons without a known birthday come last when sorting by birthday."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:354
msgid "Sort order. Defaults to ascending for the name and descending for the dates. Not used when sorting by birthday."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:359
msgid "Maximum number of persons to return."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:366
msgid "Page of results to return."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:402
msgid "Get person"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:403
msgid "Returns a single Orbis person by its post ID (post_id of the orbis-persons/search output), with the full description."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:411
msgid "Post ID of the person."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:434
msgid "Create person"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:435
msgid "Creates an Orbis person. A display name, or first names or last names, is required. Only set the fields the user provided. The current user becomes the author of the person. A comment is added to the person that logs the creation, with the AI provider and model. AI assistants must always pass their AI provider and model in the ai input. Use orbis-persons/search first to check that the person does not exist yet."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:447
msgid "The AI provider and model that created this person. AI assistants must always provide this, with the exact provider and model they run on, so that it is clear which persons were created by which AI model."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:469
msgid "Update person"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:470
msgid "Updates an Orbis person. Only the fields in the input are changed: an empty string clears a field and null clears a part of the birth date. Only change the fields the user asked for. A comment listing the changed fields is added to the person, with the AI provider and model. AI assistants must always pass their AI provider and model in the ai input. Use orbis-persons/search to find the post ID of the person."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:478
#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:519
msgid "Post ID of the person, the post_id in the orbis-persons/search output."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:488
msgid "The AI provider and model that updated this person. AI assistants must always provide this, with the exact provider and model they run on, so that it is clear which changes were made by which AI model."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:510
msgid "Comment on person"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:511
msgid "Adds a comment from the current user to an Orbis person, for example a note about a conversation with the person. AI assistants must always pass their AI provider and model in the ai input. Use orbis-persons/search to find the post ID of the person and orbis/search-comments for the existing comments of a person."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:524
msgid "Text of the comment."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:529
msgid "The AI provider and model that wrote this comment. AI assistants must always provide this, with the exact provider and model they run on, so that it is clear which comments were written by which AI model."
msgstr ""

